---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { url } from '../data/site';
const evidence = [
['Scientific leadership','Analytical strategy, pipeline development and biological interpretation across 500+ sample clinical-trial omics programs; corresponding-author work in single-cell biology and population-scale oncology RWD.'],
['Program leadership','Current direction of three oncology research programs, with operating models, milestones, research priorities, SOPs and cross-functional coordination.'],
['People & mentorship','Led four bioinformaticians at Leidos supporting CDC/NCEZID. At Georgia Tech, trained three research scientists, five graduate students and two undergraduates.'],
['Partnerships','Multi-institutional scientific coordination, vendor relationships and data-use agreements connecting research objectives with appropriate resources.'],
['Infrastructure & operations','Institutional HPC workflows, RHEL8 modules, Nextflow modernization, access coordination, reproducible pipelines and documented support processes.'],
['Grants & research strategy','Contributed to securing $1.8M for MILES and $1.7M for NIH-RMIP-IDCCH. Separately co-led a $10M+ PCF Tactical Award application; the application is not presented as awarded funding.'],
['Business & resource decisions','Evaluated $2.5M in capital equipment and vendor options for cell-characterization infrastructure. An MBA informs resource and organizational thinking; PMP certification supports structured execution.']];
---
<Site title="Scientific & Program Leadership | Bench2Bytes"><div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">LEADERSHIP</p><h1>Scientific understanding.<br />Organizational perspective.</h1><p class="lede">Connecting research questions, people, partnerships and resources so that scientific programs can move forward.</p></div><div class="leadership-evidence">{evidence.map(([title,text],i) => <section class="editorial-row"><span class="eyebrow">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / LEADERSHIP EVIDENCE</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p></section>)}</div><section class="section prose"><h2>Science × technology × business × program leadership</h2><p>Scientific depth helps define the question and interpret the evidence. Business training adds attention to priorities, trade-offs and resources. Program-management practice connects those choices with people, dependencies and execution.</p><a class="text-link" href={url('projects.html#program-leadership')}>Explore the program-leadership case →</a></section></Site>
